# ECS SCIENCE FAST PROBLEM CRACKER v1
LANGUAGE ECS_SCIENCE_FAST_CRACKER SURFACES canonical,user-native BACKENDS object,bytecode,ir-json,human

TYPE ECSEntity BASE Value
TYPE ECSComponent BASE Value
TYPE ECSProbe BASE Value
TYPE ECSResult BASE Value
TYPE ECSFrontier BASE Value

PRESERVE Provenance
PRESERVE FailureHistory
PRESERVE UnresolvedRemainder
PRESERVE EvidenceAuthorityBoundary
PRESERVE CurrentHistoricalBoundary
PRESERVE CrossDomainEvidenceSeparation

OPERATOR ECSObserve BIND ECSFrontier INPUT ECSEntity OUTPUT ECSFrontier EFFECT observe AUTHORITY none PRESERVE provenance
OPERATOR ECSDistinguish BIND ECSFrontier INPUT ECSFrontier OUTPUT ECSFrontier EFFECT analyze AUTHORITY none PRESERVE provenance
OPERATOR ECSQuotientLocal BIND ECSFrontier INPUT ECSFrontier OUTPUT ECSFrontier EFFECT representation AUTHORITY none PRESERVE query_scope evidence_boundaries
OPERATOR ECSMeasureSplit BIND ECSProbe INPUT ECSFrontier OUTPUT ECSProbe EFFECT analyze AUTHORITY none PRESERVE cost claim_ceiling
OPERATOR ECSSelectProbe BIND ECSProbe INPUT ECSFrontier OUTPUT ECSProbe EFFECT route AUTHORITY none PRESERVE cost independence discrimination
OPERATOR ECSActuate BIND ECSResult INPUT ECSProbe OUTPUT ECSResult EFFECT execute AUTHORITY none PRESERVE provenance
OPERATOR ECSVerify BIND ECSResult INPUT ECSResult OUTPUT ECSResult EFFECT verify AUTHORITY none PRESERVE claim_ceiling
OPERATOR ECSEliminateOrSplit BIND ECSFrontier INPUT ECSResult OUTPUT ECSFrontier EFFECT repair AUTHORITY none PRESERVE failures remainder
OPERATOR ECSRepeat BIND ECSFrontier INPUT ECSFrontier OUTPUT ECSFrontier EFFECT route AUTHORITY none PRESERVE lineage

RULE ECS_R01 IF "a source is ingested" THEN "do not promote it to accepted fact without verification"
RULE ECS_R02 IF "two domains use the same method" THEN "do not transfer evidence between them"
RULE ECS_R03 IF "a probe is cheap but weak" THEN "prefer the cheapest sufficiently discriminating independent probe"
RULE ECS_R04 IF "a failure occurs" THEN "retain it as evidence about the method or boundary"
RULE ECS_R05 IF "coverage is missing" THEN "record explicit remainder instead of inferring absence"
RULE ECS_R06 IF "finite execution passes" THEN "do not infer universality"
RULE ECS_R07 IF "a quotient is formed" THEN "scope equivalence to the active question"

CLAIM ECS_C01 STATUS BOUNDED_CLAIM TEXT "The fast cracker is an evidence-first ECS routing method for reducing an active DecisionField by cheap discriminating probes while preserving failures, provenance and remainder."
COUNTERPROBE "Does the selected probe actually split live alternatives after full cost is charged?"
VERIFY "No cross-domain evidence transfer, silent failure deletion, or universal claim from finite evidence."